/E (A Data Engineer is a professional responsible for designing, building, and maintaining the systems that collect, process, and store data for organizations. Their work ensures that data is reliable, accessible, and ready for analysis and decision-making.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 309 0 R
/E (Data Engineers work with raw data from multiple sources, creating ETL pipelines to extract, transform, and load data into databases and data warehouses. They ensure data quality, consistency, and performance using tools such as SQL, Python, SSIS, and cloud platforms like Azure.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 309 0 R
/E (Data Engineers also focus on data modelling, database optimization, and automation, enabling analysts and business teams to access clean, well-structured data. They collaborate closely with data analysts, data scientists, and other teams to support analytics, reporting, and scalable data solutions that drive business performance.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
