845 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (1. What is Python ETL?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (Python ETL refers to the use of Python programming to extract data from various sources, transform it into clean and structured formats, and load it into databases or analytical systems. Python is widely used in data engineering due to its simplicity, flexibility, and rich ecosystem of data processing libraries.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
847 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (2. Why Use Python for ETL?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
848 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (At a foundational level, Python is used for building lightweight, customizable ETL pipelines. It allows Data Engineers to automate data workflows, process files and API data, and apply transformation logic that may be difficult to implement using graphical tools alone. Python is especially useful for scripting, automation, and integrating diverse data sources.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
849 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (3. Data Extraction in Python)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
850 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (Data extraction involves collecting data from different sources such as CSV and Excel files, relational databases, and APIs. Using libraries like pandas, requests, and database connectors, Python enables controlled and repeatable data ingestion processes suitable for small to medium-scale workloads.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
851 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (4. Data Transformation in Python)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
852 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (During the transformation stage, raw data is cleaned, filtered, and reshaped into usable formats. Common tasks include handling missing values, converting data types, renaming columns, and applying business rules. Libraries such as pandas and numpy are commonly used to perform these operations efficiently.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
